※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4924

※ Two modules exporting one glyph for one number of operands leave nothing to decide
※ between them, so the second import is refused -- at the import, which is where the
※ choice was made, rather than at a use.
※
※ Defining the operator here instead is the way out, since what is written in this
※ file is what applies.

let a := ⎕import("one")
let b := ⎕import("other")

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(⎕drop(#(⍕1u64)), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
